00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:46.570
So that we could talk about Scott's Tots, which you directed.
这样我们就能聊聊你执导的《斯科特的托儿们》那一集了。

166
00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.810
It was your directorial debut of The Office.
那是你执导《办公室》的处女作。

167
00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:50.510
Of anything.
也是你执导的任何作品的处女作。

168
00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:50.970
Yeah.
是啊。

169
00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:54.270
Now, had you not directed a webisodes before this?
那你在这之前没执导过网络剧集吗？

170
00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.430
Oh, that's true.
噢，那是真的。

171
00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.370
I did the webisodes.
我确实做过网络剧集。

172
00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:56.750
Yeah.
是啊。

173
00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.030
But you know, the first substantial thing.
但你知道，这是第一个实质性的作品。

174
00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.590
Do you guys remember anything about the show?
你们还记得关于这部剧的任何事情吗？

175
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.010
The two of you?
你们两个？

176
00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.290
Angela, you want to just handle this on your own?
安吉拉，你想自己处理这个问题吗？

177
00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:08.850
I mean, I think you got this.
我是说，我觉得你能搞定。

178
00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:09.650
I got this.
我能搞定。

179
00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:14.470
Well, we have some stats to throw at you about some reviews of Scott's Tots.
好吧，我们有一些关于《斯科特的托儿们》的评论数据要抛给你。

180
00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:15.310
We do.
没错。

181
00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.850
Just so we get clear.
先说明白。

182
00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:20.070
Did you bring me on to answer for Scott's Tots?
你请我来是为了让我对《斯科特的托儿们》负责吗？

183
00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:20.930
No.
不是。

184
00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:22.470
Okay.
好吧。

185
00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:22.790
Okay.
好吧。

186
00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:23.250
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

187
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.210
Because I know some of this, but please, let's refresh.
因为我记得一些，但请帮我复习一下。

188
00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.170
No, not at all.
完全不是。

189
00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:27.670
Not at all.
一点也不。

190
00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:27.950
Okay.
好吧。

191
00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.670
What are they saying?
他们是怎么说的？

192
00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:36.210
Scott's Tots is widely referred to as the cringiest episode of The Office.
《斯科特的托儿们》被广泛认为是《办公室》里最让人尴尬的一集。

193
00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:42.390
The majority of our fan questions that we got for this episode were not questions at
我们收到的关于这一集的大部分粉丝提问，根本就不是问题，

194
00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:42.570
all.
完全不是。

195
00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:47.250
They were actually just comments on how cringy and uncomfortable it is for people to watch
它们其实只是评论，说人们看这一集时有多尴尬和不适，

196
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:52.350
this show, how a lot of people skip it when they do a rewatch of the show.
很多人在重温这部剧时都会跳过这一集。

197
00:07:53.050 --> 00:08:00.450
We found an article on Bustle.com that was titled this, The Scientific Reason Office
我们在Bustle.com上发现了一篇文章，标题是这样的：《为什么《办公室》粉丝

198
00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:04.730
Fans Really Can't Watch Scott's Tots, No Matter How Hard They Try.
无论如何努力都无法直视《斯科特的托儿们》的科学原因》。

199
00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.790
Oh, there's a whole article.
噢，竟然还有整整一篇文章。

200
00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.150
There's a doctor and everything.
甚至还有医生参与其中。

201
00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:08.910
Yes.
是的。

202
00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:15.750
Dr. Judith Orloff is the author of The Empath Survival Guide, and she said, quote,
朱迪斯·奥洛夫博士是《共情者生存指南》的作者，她曾引用过这样一句话：

203
00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:21.490
fans might very well avoid this episode to avoid something painful that's hard to face
粉丝们很可能会为了避免面对内心深处某种痛苦而难以直视的东西，

204
00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:22.190
in themselves.
从而选择跳过这一集。

205
00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:30.090
There is a subreddit with almost 17,000 subscribers that is titled Cannot Watch Scott's Tots.
Reddit上有一个拥有近17000名订阅者的版块，标题就是“无法观看《斯科特的托特班》”。

206
00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.590
And it is still regularly updated.
而且它至今仍会定期更新。

207
00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.970
This was my favorite.
这是我最喜欢的一条。

208
00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:35.610
What?
什么？

209
00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:45.350
One person on this subreddit said that Scott's Tots is like the moment Toby put his hand
版块里有个人说，《斯科特的托特班》就像托比把手放在帕姆膝盖上那一刻，

210
00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.350
on Pam's knee but stretched out for a whole episode.
只不过被拉长成了一整集。

211
00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:52.210
BJ, at the time, did you know?
BJ，当时你知道吗？

212
00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:56.850
Did you know that you were directing what would become the cringiest episode of The Office?
你知道你正在执导《办公室》里最让人尴尬的一集吗？

213
00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.690
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

214
00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.150
Um, it seemed great.
嗯，当时觉得挺好的。

215
00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.870
You know, I was assigned the script, loved it.
你知道，我接到了剧本，很喜欢它。

216
00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.170
Um, and it was only much later.
嗯，直到很久以后才意识到。

217
00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:17.050
I think it's a sign of how deep into the show I was or we all were, that we did not have a
我觉得这说明了当时我或者我们所有人对这部剧投入得有多深，以至于我们

218
00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:18.350
foot in the real world.
根本没法从现实角度去审视它。

219
00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:23.250
Not that it was an unrealistic episode, just that that's exactly what Michael would do.
并不是说这一集不现实，只是这确实是迈克尔会做的事。

220
00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.070
That's exactly what Michael would feel.
这确实是迈克尔会有感而发的事。

221
00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:30.750
Um, I also think that, you know, we can talk about it creatively.
嗯，我也觉得，我们可以从创作的角度来谈谈它。

222
00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:33.150
It, it makes a lot of sense to me.
对我来说，这非常合理。

223
00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:37.170
I don't know if people are responding to, it seems like no one's responding to, it's a,
我不知道大家是不是在回应，看起来没人觉得这集很烂，

224
00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:41.950
it's a bad episode or it's Michael wouldn't do that.
或者觉得迈克尔不会那样做。

225
00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.270
It's more just like, that's so hard to watch.
更多人只是觉得，这太难看下去了。

226
00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.390
So it is consistent, I think, with the show.
所以我认为，这与整部剧的基调是一致的。

227
00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:51.190
So to us, it was, it was, uh, it just made sense.
所以对我们来说，这，这，呃，这完全说得通。

228
00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:51.950
It was consistent.
它是连贯的。

229
00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:55.130
I don't remember anyone saying you can't, you can't do this.
我不记得有人说过你不能，你不能这么拍。

230
00:09:55.130 --> 00:10:02.570
But to me, I mean, it is heartbreaking, um, from both the kid's perspective, sure, but
但对我来说，它确实令人心碎，嗯，从孩子们的角度看当然是这样，但

231
00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:06.490
from Michael's perspective, which is the one you just happened to be following in the
从迈克尔的角度来看，也就是你恰好在办公室里跟随的那个人，

232
00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:13.410
office, which is that he, to me, the key to the episode was that Michael was so sure
对我而言，这一集的关键在于迈克尔是如此确信

233
00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:17.110
that he would be successful, that he could make this promise.
他会成功，确信他能兑现这个承诺。

234
00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:17.890
Yeah.
是的。

235
00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:18.330
Yeah.
是的。

236
00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:19.990
He's so believed in himself.
他对自己深信不疑。

237
00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:20.870
Yes.
没错。

238
00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:23.930
It's not, to me, it's not about the lie.
对我来说，重点不在于谎言。

239
00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.750
It's not about what ended up being a lie or a broken promise.
不在于最终变成谎言或无法兑现的承诺这件事本身。

240
00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:35.830
It's, it's Michael's, he got carried away with his generosity, his belief in himself.
而是，而是迈克尔他被自己的慷慨和自信冲昏了头脑。

241
00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:39.570
So to me, it was a very, I mean, maybe this is what people can do.
所以对我来说，这非常，我是说，也许这就是人们能做到的。

242
00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:44.810
It's a very, very lovable version of Michael Scott, as well as a heartbreaking version of
这是一个非常、非常可爱的迈克尔·斯科特版本，同时也是一个令人心碎的

243
00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.230
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特版本。

244
00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:50.970
And it's sort of the whole series in, in an incredibly distilled, uncomfortable way from
从迈克尔·斯科特的视角来看，当你这样审视它时，它几乎以一种极其浓缩、令人不适的方式

245
00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.750
the Michael Scott point of view, when you look at it like that.
概括了整部剧。

246
00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:58.990
To me, it's maybe one of the most Michael things Michael has ever done.
对我来说，这可能是迈克尔做过的最“迈克尔”的事情之一。

247
00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.070
One hundred percent.
百分之百。

248
00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.510
I love the line so much.
我太喜欢那句台词了。

249
00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:06.990
I felt like it was like everything you need to know about Michael when he says, I've made
我觉得当他说出那句“我这辈子许下过一些空头支票，但毫无疑问，那是最大方的一次”时，

250
00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.530
some empty promises in my life, but hands down, that was the most generous.
简直概括了你需要了解关于迈克尔的一切。

251
00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.030
That line is like so perfect.
那句台词简直太完美了。

252
00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:19.770
BJ, I made a list because there are a bunch of articles that list the cringiest episodes
BJ，我列了个清单，因为网上有很多文章都在盘点《办公室》里最让人尴尬的剧集，

253
00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.030
of The Office.
我把它们都列出来了。

254
00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.110
Get ready.
做好心理准备。

255
00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:24.390
You wrote most of them.
其中大部分都是你写的。

256
00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:33.530
They're Prince Family Paper, Diversity Day, Sexual Harassment, and Chair Model, all of which
分别是《普林斯家族纸业》、《多元化日》、《性骚扰》和《椅子模特》，这些全都是

257
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:34.610
you wrote.
你写的。

258
00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:35.050
Yes.
没错。

259
00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:35.850
Yes.
是的。

260
00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:43.250
Chair Model, you remember Chair Model, where Michael falls in love with a woman in a magazine
《椅子模特》，你还记得《椅子模特》吗？迈克尔爱上了一个杂志上的女人，

261
00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:47.730
and finds out she's died and he goes to her grave.
后来发现她去世了，他还去了她的墓前。

262
00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.930
It's as if he lost his wife for 50 years.
搞得好像他失去了相伴五十年的妻子一样。

263
00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:53.550
Paul Lieberstein wrote a lot.
保罗·利伯斯坦写了很多集。

264
00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.430
I love that episode.
我很喜欢那一集。

265
00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.750
Paul is the source of the darkness on that one.
保罗才是那一集黑暗风格的源头。

266
00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:02.030
And look, I wrote a lot of very joyous stuff too.
而且你看，我也写过很多非常欢乐的内容。

267
00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.110
I wrote a lot of The Jim and Pam.
我写了很多关于吉姆和帕姆的剧情。

268
00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.690
I wrote Threat Level Midnight, which is a very joyful episode.
我写了《威胁等级：午夜》，那可是非常欢乐的一集。

269
00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:14.270
So it's not like I'm the Prince of Darkness on this show.
所以并不是说我是这部剧里的“黑暗王子”。

270
00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.830
And also, look, there were what?
再说，你看，总共有多少集来着？

271
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.010
How many hundred episodes?
几百集吧？

272
00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.230
I worked on more than half of them.
我参与了其中一半以上的创作。

273
00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:25.630
So I'm not just this dark figure.
所以我不仅仅是个阴暗的角色。

274
00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:26.690
I'm proud of it.
我对此感到自豪。

275
00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.190
I'm less dark now, though.
不过我现在没那么阴暗了。

276
00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.830
Because, again, I do hear this and I do go, oh, my God.
因为再说一次，听到这些评价时，我也会想：天哪。

277
00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.470
Like, how was I capable of some of this?
我当时是怎么写出这些东西的？

278
00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:38.770
Like, especially when I when I see Ryan Howard, I'm like, oh, my God.
尤其是当我看到瑞安·霍华德的时候，我会想：天哪。

279
00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.110
Like, I don't see any villain like this.
我从没见过这样的反派。

280
00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.830
Here's the Mashable article that comes out after this episode.
这是这一集播出后Mashable网站发的一篇文章。

281
00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.630
BJ Novak, Prince of Darkness of The Office.
《BJ·诺瓦克，《办公室》的黑暗王子》。

282
00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:50.390
No, BJ.
不，BJ。

283
00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.770
We love like, my God.
我们很喜欢，天哪。

284
00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.210
No, I think the dark is important.
不，我觉得黑暗面很重要。

285
00:12:54.210 --> 00:13:04.230
And I think I think that, you know, I remember after season one, which was six episodes, and I think all of them ended pretty darkly.
而且我认为，你知道，我记得第一季之后，一共六集，我觉得每一集的结尾都挺黑暗的。

286
00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:05.230
Right.
没错。

287
00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:07.530
The pilot, Hot Girl.
试播集，《辣妹》。

288
00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:14.910
I mean, we had that nice moment at the end of Diversity, but the pilot, Diversity Day, Hot Girl, Healthcare, extremely dark.
我是说，我们在《多元化日》结尾有过温馨的时刻，但试播集、《多元化日》、《辣妹》、《医疗保健》，都极其黑暗。

289
00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:17.890
Basketball.
《篮球赛》。

290
00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:18.730
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

291
00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.130
Office Olympics and basketball maybe were a little more positive endings.
《办公室奥运会》和《篮球赛》的结局可能稍微积极一点。

292
00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:29.650
But, you know, we had sort of a big group meeting that Greg led about, OK, what are we going to do differently in season two?
但是，你知道，格雷格主持了一次大型会议，讨论我们第二季要做出什么改变。

293
00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:30.450
And there was a lot different.
确实有很多不同之处。

294
00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:37.130
And one of them was three out of four endings should be positive.
其中之一就是四集里要有三集的结局是积极的。

295
00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.950
And then one is just for us, meaning Paul.
剩下那一集就是留给我们自己的，也就是保罗。

296
00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:44.550
He was like, we're not going to totally sell out.
他的意思是，我们不能完全向市场妥协。

297
00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.150
But the British had ended dark every time, more or less.
但英版《办公室》基本上每一集的结局都是黑暗的。

298
00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.350
And we had been ending dark every time, more or less.
而我们之前也基本上每一集都以黑暗结尾。

299
00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:56.610
And so the new thing was, you know, so I guess Scott's Tots was definitely one of those four.
所以新的方针是，我想《斯科特的托特们》绝对是那四分之一里的那一集。

300
00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.490
One for us.
留给我们自己的一集。

301
00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:58.410
Yeah.
是啊。

302
00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:03.190
But again, I do think it's an interesting, it is a deep, interesting one.
但话说回来，我确实认为这是一个很有趣、很深刻的话题。

303
00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:06.430
And it's not that it's not part of the canon.
而且这并不是说它不属于正典。

304
00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.690
It is very difficult.
这非常困难。

305
00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:08.310
I agree.
我同意。

306
00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:08.810
I agree.
我同意。

307
00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.470
I think, though, it is Michael.
不过我觉得，这就是迈克尔。

308
00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:17.790
It's honestly Michael trying to do something good, believing in himself, knowing.
老实说，迈克尔是在尝试做些好事，他相信自己，他知道。

309
00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.510
Well, I don't think he knows he's going to fall short.
嗯，我不认为他知道自己会失败。

310
00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.090
Well, look how much he believes in Pam and her art.
你看他有多相信帕姆和她的艺术就知道了。

