00:42:11.390 --> 00:42:11.790
Hmm.
嗯。

902
00:42:12.030 --> 00:42:13.050
Dwight's up to something.
德怀特在搞什么名堂。

903
00:42:13.490 --> 00:42:13.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

904
00:42:14.150 --> 00:42:18.330
What he's up to is that in six hours, Jim will be fired by David Wallace.
他搞的名堂是，六小时后，吉姆就会被大卫·华莱士解雇。

905
00:42:18.570 --> 00:42:18.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

906
00:42:18.990 --> 00:42:19.230
Hmm.
嗯。

907
00:42:19.950 --> 00:42:20.090
Hmm.
嗯。

908
00:42:20.090 --> 00:42:21.630
I'm interested to see how that goes down.
我很想看看事情会怎么发展。

909
00:42:21.890 --> 00:42:22.190
Hmm.
嗯。

910
00:42:23.210 --> 00:42:25.550
Well, in the break room, Pam is eating yogurt.
好吧，在休息室里，帕姆正在吃酸奶。

911
00:42:25.550 --> 00:42:28.850
When Erin enters to ask her to look over an itinerary.
这时艾琳进来请她过目一份行程表。

912
00:42:29.630 --> 00:42:30.410
That's right.
没错。

913
00:42:30.430 --> 00:42:38.330
We had a fan catch from Kelsey in Kentucky who said, when Phyllis, Pam, and Erin are in the break room looking at the itinerary,
我们收到了一位来自肯塔基州的粉丝凯尔西的反馈，她说，当菲利斯、帕姆和艾琳在休息室看行程表时，

914
00:42:38.530 --> 00:42:42.210
it's very obvious again how much purple is in the wardrobe design.
再次非常明显地看出服装设计里用了多少紫色。

915
00:42:42.210 --> 00:42:43.110
Oh, I noticed.
哦，我注意到了。

916
00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:48.530
And later in the bullpen, you'll notice Angela Martin also has a purple lilac cardigan.
后来在办公区，你会注意到安吉拉·马丁也穿了一件紫丁香色的开衫。

917
00:42:48.670 --> 00:42:49.510
It was a purple day.
那是个紫色主题日。

918
00:42:49.750 --> 00:42:52.150
You and Kelsey are sharing a brain today.
你和凯尔西今天真是心有灵犀。

919
00:42:52.310 --> 00:42:52.670
We are.
确实。

920
00:42:52.670 --> 00:42:58.870
Well, this itinerary has one very interesting line item.
好吧，这份行程表上有一个非常有趣的条目。

921
00:42:59.330 --> 00:43:03.350
Pam is surprised to learn that the Michael Scott Foundation is still in existence.
帕姆惊讶地发现迈克尔·斯科特基金会竟然还存在。

922
00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:06.370
And Phyllis says, what's Scott's tots?
菲利斯问，斯科特的小崽子们是什么？

923
00:43:06.370 --> 00:43:11.070
And Stanley starts laughing and says, has it really been 10 years?
斯坦利开始大笑，说，真的过去十年了吗？

924
00:43:11.070 --> 00:43:13.250
I mean, Stanley isn't just laughing.
我是说，斯坦利不仅仅是在笑。

925
00:43:13.250 --> 00:43:19.770
It is a laugh that comes, like, from a deep place of like, oh, this guy is screwed.
那笑声仿佛来自内心深处，就像是，噢，这家伙死定了。

926
00:43:19.970 --> 00:43:22.390
And I am thrilled to watch it happen.
我很兴奋能看到这一幕发生。

927
00:43:22.990 --> 00:43:26.150
Well, Stanley's going to hold up a newspaper.
好吧，斯坦利会举起一份报纸。

928
00:43:26.490 --> 00:43:31.570
The headline reads, local businessman pledges college tuition to third graders.
头条写着，当地商人承诺资助三年级学生大学学费。

929
00:43:32.770 --> 00:43:35.310
We kind of talked about this with BJ a little bit.
我们之前和BJ稍微聊过这个。

930
00:43:35.530 --> 00:43:39.590
And we got a fan mail flurry about this newspaper article that Stanley's holding up.
我们收到了一大堆关于斯坦利举着的那份报纸的粉丝来信。

931
00:43:39.750 --> 00:43:40.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

932
00:43:41.070 --> 00:43:43.350
Because it looks like the real Scranton Times.
因为它看起来就像真的《斯克兰顿时报》。

933
00:43:43.670 --> 00:43:44.590
It really does.
确实很像。

934
00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:47.210
This is fakie filet, but it's done amazingly.
这是伪造的，但做得太棒了。

935
00:43:47.530 --> 00:43:51.210
It is actually a real Scranton Times newspaper.
它实际上是一份真实的《斯克兰顿时报》。

936
00:43:52.030 --> 00:43:55.350
Randy Cordray explained how we made this amazing prop.
兰迪·科德雷解释了我们是如何制作这个惊人道具的。

937
00:43:55.910 --> 00:44:00.350
So first, they hired a group of kids to take a picture with Michael Scott at school.
首先，他们雇了一群孩子在学校和迈克尔·斯科特合影。

938
00:44:00.710 --> 00:44:05.990
And Kim Ferry even styled Steve's hair in a retro Caesar-style hairdo.
金·费里甚至给史蒂夫设计了一个复古的凯撒式发型。

939
00:44:06.130 --> 00:44:10.110
You know that one that was made popular by George Clooney in the early years of ER?
你知道那种在《急诊室的故事》早期由乔治·克鲁尼带火的发型吗？

940
00:44:10.110 --> 00:44:11.150
Oh, yes.
哦，知道。

941
00:44:11.250 --> 00:44:11.510
Yes.
是的。

942
00:44:11.710 --> 00:44:14.150
I mean, that's how detailed they were about this photo.
我是说，他们对这张照片的细节要求有多高。

943
00:44:14.290 --> 00:44:15.910
They think Michael Scott would be into this hairdo.
他们认为迈克尔·斯科特会喜欢这种发型。

944
00:44:16.370 --> 00:44:23.270
So then Phil Shea contacted the Scranton Times and asked for a copy of their newspaper from 10 years ago.
所以菲尔·谢伊联系了《斯克兰顿时报》，索要了一份十年前的报纸副本。

945
00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:31.430
And when he was looking through it, he said, do you think you would be willing to reproduce the local page?
当他翻看时，他说，你们愿意重新印制一下地方版面吗？

946
00:44:31.450 --> 00:44:39.950
So not the front page, but the local page with a different feature story at the bottom of the page so that we can use it on our show.
不是头版，而是地方版面，并在页面底部换上一篇专题报道，这样我们就能在剧里用了。

947
00:44:41.730 --> 00:44:48.130
So the writers wrote a fake article, and Randy Shemansky, who worked at the Times, put it all together.
于是编剧们写了一篇假文章，在《时报》工作的兰迪·谢曼斯基把它整合在了一起。

948
00:44:48.130 --> 00:44:52.910
He put his name as the writer in the byline and printed it for us.
他把自己的名字作为作者写在署名栏里，并为我们印了出来。

949
00:44:53.310 --> 00:44:54.290
Nice, Randy.
干得好，兰迪。

950
00:44:54.510 --> 00:44:55.190
Thank you.
谢谢。

951
00:44:55.690 --> 00:44:57.470
Well, that's why it looks so real.
嗯，这就是为什么它看起来那么真实。

952
00:44:57.690 --> 00:44:57.950
Yeah.
是啊。

953
00:44:57.950 --> 00:45:03.390
Well, there's photos of it online, and there's also some on Office Tally, and I'll put some of those in our stories.
网上有相关照片，Office Tally网站上也有一些，我会把其中一些放到我们的快拍里。

954
00:45:03.670 --> 00:45:04.070
Yes.
好的。

955
00:45:04.230 --> 00:45:10.930
The entire text of the article is on officetally.com, and I thought I would read one of my favorite passages.
这篇文章的全文都在officetally.com上，我想读一下我最喜欢的一段。

956
00:45:11.070 --> 00:45:12.470
The whole thing is worth a read.
整篇文章都值得一读。

957
00:45:13.410 --> 00:45:17.430
But this one really goes with the episode.
但这一段真的和这集内容很契合。

958
00:45:17.830 --> 00:45:18.750
It says,
上面写着，

959
00:45:19.070 --> 00:45:23.730
Talib Johnson, a student in Alice Kay's class, has dreams of becoming a doctor.
爱丽丝·凯班里的学生塔利布·约翰逊梦想成为一名医生。

960
00:45:24.450 --> 00:45:32.850
Talib's mother has already been trying to save for the daunting $120,000 cost of medical school, and she was not sure if it could ever be a reality.
塔利布的母亲一直在努力为医学院那高昂的12万美元学费攒钱，她不确定这是否能成为现实。

961
00:45:33.250 --> 00:45:41.550
But now that Scott has offered to pick up the tab, Mrs. Johnson said that Talib would undoubtedly be going to an Ivy League university.
但现在斯科特主动提出承担这笔费用，约翰逊夫人说塔利布无疑将进入常春藤盟校学习。

962
00:45:42.550 --> 00:45:43.630
That's in the article.
这就是文章里的内容。

963
00:45:43.890 --> 00:45:44.890
It's very on theme.
非常贴合主题。

964
00:45:44.910 --> 00:45:45.670
I know.
我知道。

965
00:45:46.090 --> 00:45:49.250
Well, Jenna, I have a little section I'm calling According to the Internet.
珍娜，我有个小板块叫“据互联网所说”。

966
00:45:49.890 --> 00:45:50.450
Oh.
哦。

967
00:45:50.690 --> 00:45:50.990
Yeah.
是啊。

968
00:45:51.190 --> 00:45:54.570
When you type in Scott's Tots, lots of stuff comes up.
当你输入“斯科特的托特们”时，会出现很多相关内容。

969
00:45:54.690 --> 00:45:56.130
I'm going to share three with you.
我要和你分享三条。

970
00:45:56.610 --> 00:46:04.010
The first one is, According to the Internet, you might ask yourself, how much money would Michael have to pay for all of their tuition?
第一条是，据互联网所说，你可能会问自己，迈克尔到底要为他们所有人的学费支付多少钱？

971
00:46:04.430 --> 00:46:04.830
Oh.
哦。

972
00:46:05.290 --> 00:46:10.250
Assuming all 15 of Scott's Tots attended a four-year private university,
假设所有15个“斯科特的托特们”都上了四年制私立大学，

973
00:46:10.250 --> 00:46:14.850
Michael would probably have to pay something around $1.9 million.
迈克尔可能需要支付大约190万美元。

974
00:46:15.890 --> 00:46:16.450
Wow.
哇。

975
00:46:17.170 --> 00:46:17.710
Yeah.
是啊。

976
00:46:17.990 --> 00:46:25.290
So when he made this promise 10 years ago, he believed he would have so much money that he'd have like an extra $2 million.
所以当他在10年前做出这个承诺时，他以为自己到时候会有很多钱，多出个200万美元左右。

977
00:46:25.470 --> 00:46:25.910
That's right.
没错。

978
00:46:26.710 --> 00:46:34.850
Number two, if you go to Oklahoma State University in Stillwater, Oklahoma, you can join a student club called Scott's Tots.
第二条，如果你去俄克拉荷马州斯蒂尔沃特的俄克拉荷马州立大学，你可以加入一个叫“斯科特的托特们”的学生社团。

979
00:46:35.130 --> 00:46:36.630
What does Scott's Tots do?
“斯科特的托特们”是做什么的？

980
00:46:36.630 --> 00:46:42.670
According to the online newspaper of the school, The O'Collee, staff reporter Jake Sellers wrote,
据该校在线校报《The O'Collee》报道，特约记者杰克·塞勒斯写道，

981
00:46:42.670 --> 00:46:49.150
Members of the Scott's Tots Club meet weekly to stream and test their knowledge on NBC's The Office.
“斯科特的托特们”社团成员每周聚会，观看NBC的《办公室》并测试他们对剧集的了解程度。

982
00:46:49.450 --> 00:46:55.790
This semester, the club started fresh, mostly meeting in classroom building on Wednesdays, and it goes on to say,
本学期，该社团重新开始活动，主要在周三于教学楼聚会，文中还说，

983
00:46:55.970 --> 00:47:01.710
Although this club may be a time for some students to watch a show, for some it is a time to connect.
虽然这个社团对一些学生来说可能是看剧的时间，但对另一些人来说，这是建立联系的时间。

984
00:47:02.370 --> 00:47:06.730
Haley McCauley, senior business manager, is the secretary of Scott's Tots.
高级商务经理海莉·麦考利是“斯科特的托特们”的秘书。

985
00:47:07.170 --> 00:47:14.810
McCauley joined in the fall of her freshman year, and she says they have trivia nights with prizes for the winners, and, quote, she says,
麦考利在大一秋季加入，她说他们有知识竞赛之夜，获胜者有奖品，而且，引用她的话说，

986
00:47:15.010 --> 00:47:16.170
It's a really fun club.
“这是一个非常有趣的社团。”

987
00:47:16.630 --> 00:47:16.970
Hmm.
嗯。

988
00:47:17.370 --> 00:47:20.490
The article also included a flyer they had made for their club.
文章里还附带了他们为社团制作的传单。

989
00:47:20.690 --> 00:47:21.810
I'm going to put it in our stories.
我会把它放到我们的快拍里。

990
00:47:22.350 --> 00:47:23.330
Oh, I love it.
哦，我喜欢这个。

991
00:47:23.350 --> 00:47:25.450
It's got a gym face on it and a dundee.
上面有吉姆的脸和邓迪奖杯。

992
00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:31.030
Yeah, and the stapler in the Jell-O, it says, it has their campus link, and this is what it says,
对，还有果冻里的订书机，上面写着他们的校园链接，内容是这样的，

993
00:47:31.150 --> 00:47:33.990
We watch The Office Show and have trivia nights once a month.
“我们观看《办公室》剧集，每月举办一次知识竞赛之夜。”

994
00:47:34.130 --> 00:47:35.530
We have snacks!
“我们有零食！”

995
00:47:36.750 --> 00:47:38.310
Well, you and I are going.
好吧，你和我得去参加一下。

996
00:47:38.470 --> 00:47:38.950
I know.
我知道。

997
00:47:39.110 --> 00:47:40.870
And then it says where you can join to be a member.
然后上面写着加入成为会员的方式。

998
00:47:41.270 --> 00:47:51.270
And according to the internet number three, I found a ton, like too many to list, youth soccer teams named Scott's Tots all across the United States.
而据互联网所说第三条，我发现全美各地有大量的，多到数不清的青少年足球队都叫“斯科特的托特们”。

999
00:47:51.610 --> 00:47:52.050
Wow.
哇。

1000
00:47:52.050 --> 00:47:52.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1001
00:47:52.750 --> 00:47:57.070
You can go cheer on Scott's Tots at almost any soccer field on a Saturday in America.
在美国，几乎每个周六，你都能在足球场上看到为“斯科特的小宝贝们”加油助威的人。

1002
00:47:57.270 --> 00:48:06.210
So that's some stuff I found on the internet, but we should go back to the break room because Pam has a very different reaction than Stanley to this information.
以上就是我在网上找到的一些内容，但我们还是回到休息室吧，因为帕姆对这些信息的反应和斯坦利截然不同。

1003
00:48:06.670 --> 00:48:10.770
I mean, Pam uses the word terrible, like, five times.
我是说，帕姆用了大概五次“太糟糕了”这个词。

1004
00:48:10.930 --> 00:48:11.090
Yeah.
没错。

1005
00:48:11.710 --> 00:48:14.230
She feels like she's not getting through to Michael.
她觉得她没法和迈克尔沟通。

1006
00:48:14.390 --> 00:48:17.170
She's like, Why would you promise something like that?
她就像是在说，你怎么能做出那种承诺呢？

1007
00:48:17.330 --> 00:48:19.530
This is a terrible thing, Michael.
迈克尔，这太糟糕了。

1008
00:48:19.730 --> 00:48:20.950
This is terrible.
这太糟糕了。

1009
00:48:20.950 --> 00:48:22.390
It's just terrible.
简直太糟糕了。

1010
00:48:22.750 --> 00:48:24.990
And she's like, You have to go tell them now.
她还说，你现在必须去告诉他们真相。

1011
00:48:25.670 --> 00:48:33.370
Did you see the article, Angela, where it sort of broke down there are two reactions to this episode from viewers.
安吉拉，你看到那篇文章了吗？它分析了观众对这一集的两种反应。

1012
00:48:33.370 --> 00:48:36.210
You're either a Stanley or a Pam.
你要么是斯坦利型，要么是帕姆型。

1013
00:48:36.510 --> 00:48:41.490
Like it was saying, you're either a person who laughs through tragedy.
就像文章里说的，你要么是那种在悲剧中也能笑出来的人。

1014
00:48:41.770 --> 00:48:41.970
Yeah.
没错。

1015
00:48:41.970 --> 00:48:44.810
You know, you're that person at the funeral who gets the giggles.
你知道的，就是葬礼上那种会忍不住偷笑的人。

1016
00:48:45.090 --> 00:48:45.270
Right.
对。

1017
00:48:45.470 --> 00:48:48.390
Or you have no sense of humor about it.
要么就是对此完全没有幽默感的人。

1018
00:48:48.650 --> 00:48:53.130
They were sort of saying, like, if you're a Pam, you probably can't watch this episode.
文章里大概是说，如果你是帕姆型，你可能根本没法看这一集。

1019
00:48:53.450 --> 00:48:53.670
Right.
对。

1020
00:48:53.950 --> 00:48:55.890
It's a really interesting article, actually.
说实话，那篇文章真的很有意思。

1021
00:48:55.890 --> 00:48:57.370
It's on decider.com.
在decider.com上。

1022
00:48:57.770 --> 00:49:00.090
And I don't know which one I am.
我不知道自己属于哪一种。

1023
00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:02.010
I mean, I have a visceral reaction.
我是说，我的反应很直观。

1024
00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:03.610
Like, I feel so bad for these kids.
比如，我真的为这些孩子感到难过。

1025
00:49:03.610 --> 00:49:07.610
And I also see Stanley finally getting to see Michael get his comeuppance.
但同时，我也看到斯坦利终于目睹了迈克尔自食其果。

1026
00:49:08.270 --> 00:49:08.570
Yes.
没错。

1027
00:49:09.270 --> 00:49:11.230
I don't know which one I am either.
我也不知道我是哪种人。

1028
00:49:11.470 --> 00:49:12.610
I enjoyed this episode.
我很喜欢这一集。

1029
00:49:12.610 --> 00:49:14.830
So I guess I must be a little Stanley.
所以我猜我可能有一点斯坦利的特质。

1030
00:49:15.710 --> 00:49:16.930
Maybe we're a combo.
也许我们是两者的结合体。

1031
00:49:17.450 --> 00:49:18.910
I don't know who that would be.
我不知道那会是什么样。

1032
00:49:19.070 --> 00:49:20.070
Are you an Aaron then?
那你是个亚伦型吗？

1033
00:49:20.830 --> 00:49:22.470
Aaron seems horrified.
亚伦看起来被吓坏了。

1034
00:49:22.710 --> 00:49:27.810
And yet also, she still finds a positive spin at the end.
但即便如此，她最后还是找到了积极的一面。

1035
00:49:28.250 --> 00:49:29.490
Yeah, maybe we're Aaron.
没错，也许我们是亚伦型。

1036
00:49:29.950 --> 00:49:34.890
The article said about people who are Stanleys, and I thought this was worded really well.
文章里提到了斯坦利型的人，我觉得那段话写得非常好。

1037
00:49:35.090 --> 00:49:36.410
They're not heartless.
他们并非铁石心肠。

1038
00:49:36.410 --> 00:49:39.510
They're almost shocked to the point of hilarity.
他们只是被震惊到了，以至于觉得滑稽可笑。

1039
00:49:39.750 --> 00:49:40.270
Right.
对。

1040
00:49:40.530 --> 00:49:44.570
When something is so insanely absurd to you that someone could do that, that you're like,
当某件事荒谬到让你觉得不可思议，让你不禁想问：

1041
00:49:44.610 --> 00:49:44.830
what?
什么？

1042
00:49:45.710 --> 00:49:47.130
That's their coping mechanism.
那就是他们的应对机制。

1043
00:49:47.310 --> 00:49:47.510
Yeah.
没错。

1044
00:49:47.850 --> 00:49:48.130
Right.
对。

1045
00:49:48.730 --> 00:49:51.070
Whereas Pam, it's just all just torturous.
而对于帕姆来说，这一切简直就是折磨。

1046
00:49:51.790 --> 00:49:52.310
Yeah.
没错。

1047
00:49:53.270 --> 00:49:59.050
Well, I was really disappointed because I didn't get to go with Michael.
其实我挺失望的，因为我没能和迈克尔一起去。

1048
00:49:59.050 --> 00:50:06.770
As an actor, I wanted to see Pam take Michael to this moment in his life.
作为演员，我想看帕姆陪迈克尔经历他人生中的这一刻。

1049
00:50:07.330 --> 00:50:09.350
But Pam refuses to go.
但帕姆拒绝去了。

1050
00:50:10.390 --> 00:50:11.950
Aaron's going to have to do it.
亚伦只能自己去了。

1051
00:50:12.090 --> 00:50:15.090
But I was very jealous as an actor.
但我作为演员当时非常嫉妒。

1052
00:50:15.330 --> 00:50:19.210
That you didn't get to go spend the day with Steve and watch him do these amazing scenes.
嫉妒你没能和史蒂夫一起度过那一天，看他演那些精彩的戏份。

1053
00:50:19.430 --> 00:50:19.670
Yes.
没错。

1054
00:50:20.190 --> 00:50:22.490
Well, Michael now has this famous talking head.
好吧，迈克尔现在有了这个著名的采访镜头。

1055
00:50:22.610 --> 00:50:26.650
We talked about it a little bit with BJ, where he says, I just, you know, I fell in love with
我们和BJ稍微聊过这个，他说，我只是，你知道，我爱上了

1056
00:50:26.650 --> 00:50:27.250
those kids.
那些孩子。

1057
00:50:27.710 --> 00:50:29.290
And so he made him a promise.
所以他向他们许下了一个承诺。

1058
00:50:29.450 --> 00:50:30.470
He wanted to help them.
他想帮助他们。

1059
00:50:30.670 --> 00:50:34.550
He wanted to see them graduate from high school and he would pay for their college.
他想看着他们高中毕业，并承诺会资助他们上大学。

1060
00:50:34.550 --> 00:50:41.150
Yes, this is sort of the explanation behind this predicament, behind the premise for this
是的，这算是对这一困境的解释，也是这一集

1061
00:50:41.150 --> 00:50:41.710
episode.
前提的由来。

1062
00:50:41.970 --> 00:50:46.510
We got a fan question from Aaron in Oxford, Ohio, who said this,
我们收到了一位来自俄亥俄州牛津市的粉丝亚伦的提问，他是这么说的：

1063
00:50:47.030 --> 00:50:53.590
I recently watched The Big Lebowski and there is a specific scene that caught my eye.
我最近看了《谋杀绿脚趾》，有一个特定的场景引起了我的注意。

1064
00:50:53.950 --> 00:50:58.330
In the scene, the dude is visiting Mr. Lebowski's house.
在那一幕里，老兄去拜访勒博斯基先生的家。

1065
00:50:58.770 --> 00:51:03.890
During the visit, he's given a tour of the study and notices a picture on the wall of Mr.
在拜访期间，他参观了书房，注意到墙上有一张照片，上面是勒博斯基先生

1066
00:51:03.890 --> 00:51:07.810
Lebowski surrounded by a bunch of smiling high school age children.
被一群面带微笑的高中生簇拥着。

1067
00:51:08.130 --> 00:51:13.050
The dude asks, oh, are those Mr. Lebowski's children?
老兄问，哦，那是勒博斯基先生的孩子吗？

1068
00:51:13.370 --> 00:51:17.490
To which the butler replies, they're not literally his children.
管家回答说，他们并不是他亲生的孩子。

1069
00:51:17.750 --> 00:51:22.310
They're the little Lebowski urban achievers, inner city children of promise, but without
他们是“小勒博斯基城市成就者”，是城里有前途的孩子，但缺乏

1070
00:51:22.310 --> 00:51:24.610
the necessary means for a higher education.
接受高等教育的必要经济条件。

1071
00:51:24.890 --> 00:51:28.950
So Mr. Lebowski has committed to sending all of them to college.
所以勒博斯基先生承诺资助他们所有人上大学。

1072
00:51:29.530 --> 00:51:33.810
My question is, did the writers have it in their head that Michael,
我的问题是，编剧们在构思时是否想到迈克尔

1073
00:51:33.810 --> 00:51:40.570
saw this movie and that this might have led him to making a similar promise, or is it just
看过这部电影，并因此做出了类似的承诺，还是这仅仅是一个

1074
00:51:40.570 --> 00:51:41.490
a coincidence?
巧合？

1075
00:51:42.430 --> 00:51:44.170
I had to find out.
我必须弄清楚。

1076
00:51:44.530 --> 00:51:50.290
So I reached out to Gene and Lee, who wrote this episode, and they said that the idea
所以我联系了这一集的编剧吉恩和李，他们说这一集的构思

1077
00:51:50.290 --> 00:51:54.990
for this episode actually came from Paul Lieberstein.
实际上来自保罗·利伯斯坦。

1078
00:51:55.670 --> 00:52:00.690
Paul confirmed this, and when I asked him if the idea was inspired by The Big Lebowski,
保罗证实了这一点，当我问他这个想法是否受《谋杀绿脚趾》启发时，

1079
00:52:00.690 --> 00:52:04.510
he said no, that he wasn't even aware of that scene in the movie.
他说没有，他甚至都不知道电影里有那个场景。

1080
00:52:04.970 --> 00:52:10.610
Paul said that there was a real story of a businessman who did this with extraordinary
保罗说，确实有一个真实故事，讲的是一位商人在20世纪90年代

1081
00:52:10.610 --> 00:52:13.050
success back in the 1990s.
成功地做了这件事。

1082
00:52:13.130 --> 00:52:15.330
He thinks maybe it was Chicago.
他觉得可能是在芝加哥。

1083
00:52:15.330 --> 00:52:16.690
He couldn't quite remember.
他记不太清了。

1084
00:52:17.170 --> 00:52:20.910
But it was a high school where the graduation rate was incredibly low.
但那是一所高中，毕业率极低。

1085
00:52:21.150 --> 00:52:26.370
But within the group of kids that he made this promise to, all of them went to college.
但在他做出承诺的那群孩子中，所有人都上了大学。

1086
00:52:26.370 --> 00:52:34.210
And Paul just remembered the photo in the newspaper, and he said that seems like something Michael
保罗只记得报纸上的那张照片，他说这看起来像是迈克尔·斯科特

1087
00:52:34.210 --> 00:52:40.410
Scott would do, that Michael, because of his good heart and being so sure that he would
会做的事，因为迈克尔心地善良，而且深信等这些孩子毕业时他已经

1088
00:52:40.410 --> 00:52:46.990
be a millionaire by the time these kids graduated, that he would want to help and he would make
成了百万富翁，所以他会想要帮忙，并做出

1089
00:52:46.990 --> 00:52:48.190
this promise.
这个承诺。

1090
00:52:48.190 --> 00:52:53.230
He said, quote, it felt like a really honest problem coming from this character.
他说，引用原话，“这感觉像是这个角色会遇到的一个非常真实的问题。”

1091
00:52:53.890 --> 00:52:59.710
So that was the inspiration, was this article that he had seen of someone doing this successfully
所以灵感来源就是他看到的这篇关于某人成功做到此事的文章，

1092
00:52:59.710 --> 00:53:04.250
and thinking, Michael Scott wouldn't do it successfully, though, would he?
然后心想，迈克尔·斯科特可做不到这么成功，对吧？

1093
00:53:04.250 --> 00:53:06.910
He'd want to do it, but he wouldn't be able to follow through.
他会想去做，但他无法坚持到底。

1094
00:53:07.170 --> 00:53:07.410
Yeah.
没错。

1095
00:53:07.550 --> 00:53:10.970
So he said the idea was his, but Lee and Gene made it their own.
所以他说构思是他的，但李和吉恩把它变成了他们自己的东西。

1096
00:53:11.110 --> 00:53:13.270
They came up with the dance, the batteries.
他们想出了跳舞和电池的桥段。

1097
00:53:13.270 --> 00:53:14.810
He said that was all them.
他说那全是他们的功劳。

1098
00:53:15.030 --> 00:53:18.950
But that was the inspiration behind Scott's Tots.
但这就是“斯科特的学童”这一集的灵感来源。

1099
00:53:19.570 --> 00:53:20.170
Well, I love that.
嗯，我喜欢这个。

1100
00:53:20.250 --> 00:53:22.430
I always love finding out the inspiration for our episodes.
我一直很喜欢挖掘我们剧集背后的灵感来源。

1101
00:53:22.810 --> 00:53:25.630
It's usually some little thing that just stuck with someone.
通常是一些小事，让人难以忘怀。

1102
00:53:25.850 --> 00:53:26.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1103
00:53:26.550 --> 00:53:31.090
Meanwhile, in the kitchen, Dwight is continuing to act strange.
与此同时，在厨房里，德怀特继续表现得很奇怪。

1104
00:53:32.130 --> 00:53:32.650
Yeah.
没错。

1105
00:53:33.450 --> 00:53:35.910
He's showering Jim with compliments.
他一直在对吉姆大加赞赏。

1106
00:53:35.910 --> 00:53:42.730
And then he provides him with a spreadsheet so that Jim can rank everyone based on performance
然后他给了吉姆一张电子表格，让吉姆根据表现给每个人排名，

1107
00:53:42.730 --> 00:53:44.830
for his Employee of the Month project.
为了他的“月度最佳员工”项目。

1108
00:53:45.310 --> 00:53:48.590
He says he'll run it over to Toby and the accounting department.
他说他会把表格送到托比和会计部门。

1109
00:53:48.770 --> 00:53:51.650
So it'll just be like totally impartial.
这样就完全公正了。

1110
00:53:51.770 --> 00:53:52.530
They'll run the data.
他们会处理这些数据。

1111
00:53:52.790 --> 00:53:53.290
Exactly.
没错。

1112
00:53:53.690 --> 00:53:54.450
Just database.
纯粹的数据处理。

1113
00:53:54.970 --> 00:53:55.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1114
00:53:55.710 --> 00:54:00.710
Did you notice during this scene what Rain took out of the fridge at the beginning?
你注意到这一幕开头雷恩从冰箱里拿出了什么吗？

1115
00:54:00.710 --> 00:54:05.530
Like his excuse for going into the kitchen is to get something out of the fridge, to run
他去厨房的借口是去冰箱拿东西，好去

1116
00:54:05.530 --> 00:54:06.010
into Jim?
撞见吉姆？

1117
00:54:06.350 --> 00:54:06.870
No.
没注意。

1118
00:54:07.090 --> 00:54:07.790
What was it?
是什么？

1119
00:54:08.210 --> 00:54:08.730
Mustard.
芥末酱。

1120
00:54:09.050 --> 00:54:10.490
What's he doing with mustard?
他拿芥末酱干什么？

1121
00:54:10.750 --> 00:54:11.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

1122
00:54:11.810 --> 00:54:12.910
Did he do anything with it?
他用它做了什么吗？

1123
00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:16.810
He does nothing with the mustard, but when they pull back wide, there are more things
他什么也没做，但当镜头拉远时，台面上还有更多他从冰箱里拿出来的东西。

1124
00:54:16.810 --> 00:54:19.330
on the counter that he has gotten out of the fridge.
他还拿了果酱，我想还有烧烤酱。

1125
00:54:19.750 --> 00:54:24.010
He also got out jelly and I think barbecue sauce.
真恶心。

1126
00:54:24.370 --> 00:54:24.890
Gross.
所以我想他绝对是沉迷于调味品了。

1127
00:54:25.370 --> 00:54:30.050
So he's definitely, I guess, heavy in the condiments.
果酱算是调味品吗？

1128
00:54:30.710 --> 00:54:32.630
Is jelly a condiment?
果酱是调味品吗？

1129
00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:34.610
Is jelly a condiment?
我是说，你把它涂在……黄油算调味品吗？

1130
00:54:34.830 --> 00:54:37.550
I mean, you put it on, is butter a condiment?
我觉得不算。

1131
00:54:37.870 --> 00:54:38.790
I'm going to say no.
那什么是调味品？

1132
00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:39.810
What is a condiment?
调味品不就是，嗯，我想，不就是那些额外添加的东西吗？

1133
00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:44.230
Isn't a condiment like, well, I guess, isn't it like the extras?
所以也许你是对的。

1134
00:54:44.450 --> 00:54:45.290
So maybe you're right.
我是说，到底什么是调味品？

1135
00:54:45.610 --> 00:54:48.770
I mean, what is a condiment?
比如盐和胡椒？

1136
00:54:49.090 --> 00:54:50.250
Like salt and pepper?
不，那是香料。

1137
00:54:50.590 --> 00:54:51.730
No, that's a spice.
抱歉。

1138
00:54:54.150 --> 00:54:55.090
I'm sorry.
调味品的定义是用来给食物增加风味的物质，比如盐或番茄酱。

1139
00:54:55.800 --> 00:55:01.530
The definition of condiment is a substance such as salt or ketchup that is used to add
谢谢你。

1140
00:55:01.530 --> 00:55:02.710
flavor to food.
香料也算调味品？

1141
00:55:02.850 --> 00:55:03.530
Thank you.
看看是谁说对了。

1142
00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:05.390
Spices are condiments?
我找到了一张列出不同调味品热量的图表。

1143
00:55:05.750 --> 00:55:07.850
Look who was right about something.
你知道蜂蜜也被认为是调味品吗？

1144
00:55:08.330 --> 00:55:12.730
I found a chart that lists the calories in different condiments.
好吧，现在说得通了。

1145
00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:15.510
Did you know honey is considered a condiment?
他们把意面酱也列为调味品。

1146
00:55:15.730 --> 00:55:16.830
Well, that makes sense now.
它能提升风味。

1147
00:55:17.470 --> 00:55:20.290
They're listing marinara as a condiment.
什么都能提升风味。

1148
00:55:20.290 --> 00:55:21.890
It enhances flavor.
洋葱也能提升风味。

1149
00:55:22.790 --> 00:55:24.550
Everything enhances flavor.
洋葱也能提升风味。

1150
00:55:24.730 --> 00:55:26.910
An onion enhances flavor.
洋葱也能提升风味。

1151
00:55:27.110 --> 00:55:27.490
Garlic.
大蒜。

1152
00:55:28.350 --> 00:55:29.890
Does it have to be?
非得是这个吗？

1153
00:55:30.130 --> 00:55:32.070
Do you have to squeeze it out of a bottle?
非得是从瓶子里挤出来的吗？

1154
00:55:32.270 --> 00:55:32.890
Does it have to be?
非得是这样吗？

1155
00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:33.150
Yeah.
没错。

1156
00:55:33.510 --> 00:55:34.590
Does it have to be in something?
非得加在什么东西里吗？

1157
00:55:35.690 --> 00:55:37.050
What is a condiment?
什么是调味品？

1158
00:55:37.570 --> 00:55:39.390
I need more information.
我需要更多信息。

1159
00:55:39.710 --> 00:55:41.410
We need more information on condiments.
我们需要更多关于调味品的信息。

1160
00:55:42.150 --> 00:55:42.910
Hold on.
等等。

1161
00:55:42.910 --> 00:55:46.330
Is jelly a condiment?
果冻是调味品吗？

1162
00:55:47.870 --> 00:55:53.530
Jelly and jam are usually viewed as condiments, but peanut butter is not.
果冻和果酱通常被视为调味品，但花生酱不是。

1163
00:55:54.630 --> 00:55:59.390
Salsa is considered a condiment, but guacamole is not.
莎莎酱被认为是调味品，但牛油果酱不是。

1164
00:55:59.590 --> 00:56:00.310
Here's what I'm thinking.
我是这么想的。

1165
00:56:00.490 --> 00:56:04.810
Condiments either have to be something you sprinkle or like kind of more of a liquidy form.
调味品要么是撒上去的东西，要么是某种液态形式。

1166
00:56:05.150 --> 00:56:11.850
Not according to Wikipedia, which says a condiment is a supplemental food such as a sauce or powder.
维基百科可不是这么说的，它说调味品是像酱汁或粉末之类的辅助食品。

1167
00:56:13.310 --> 00:56:14.430
Sprinkle and liquid.
撒上去的和液体的。

1168
00:56:15.270 --> 00:56:16.610
That supports my theory.
这支持了我的理论。

1169
00:56:17.750 --> 00:56:20.230
If it's more of a solid substance, it's not a condiment.
如果它是固体物质，那它就不是调味品。

1170
00:56:20.550 --> 00:56:22.690
If you can sprinkle it or pour it, it's a condiment.
如果你能撒上去或倒出来，它就是调味品。

1171
00:56:22.690 --> 00:56:24.650
If you can chop it, it's not a condiment.
如果你能切开它，它就不是调味品。

1172
00:56:25.370 --> 00:56:26.350
Sprinkle and pour.
撒和倒。

1173
00:56:26.950 --> 00:56:27.530
All right.
好吧。

1174
00:56:27.750 --> 00:56:29.830
Are we ready to move on from the condiments?
我们准备好结束调味品的话题了吗？

1175
00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:31.230
Maybe.
也许吧。

1176
00:56:31.670 --> 00:56:32.110
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1177
00:56:33.870 --> 00:56:35.370
My God, you're making a lot of hmm.
天哪，你一直在发出“嗯”的声音。

1178
00:56:35.730 --> 00:56:36.610
It sounds like, you know what?
听起来就像是，你知道吗？

1179
00:56:36.730 --> 00:56:37.270
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1180
00:56:37.450 --> 00:56:37.810
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1181
00:56:37.810 --> 00:56:39.950
When you do that, it means you disagree.
当你那样做的时候，意味着你不同意。

1182
00:56:39.950 --> 00:56:40.770
Like, hmm.
就像是，嗯。

1183
00:56:41.510 --> 00:56:42.030
Icing.
糖霜。

1184
00:56:43.090 --> 00:56:44.610
Icing is a condiment?
糖霜是调味品？

1185
00:56:44.910 --> 00:56:49.150
So when I'm eating a cupcake, I'm eating cake with a condiment on top?
所以当我吃纸杯蛋糕时，我是在吃上面加了调味品的蛋糕？

1186
00:56:49.270 --> 00:56:50.230
Makes sense to me.
我觉得说得通。

1187
00:56:50.810 --> 00:56:51.290
Really?
真的吗？

1188
00:56:51.810 --> 00:56:52.810
Jenna's doing it.
珍娜就在这么做。

1189
00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:53.190
Hmm.
嗯。

1190
00:56:53.370 --> 00:56:54.390
I knew it.
我就知道。

1191
00:56:56.540 --> 00:56:59.780
If you're ever in a conversation with Jenna, she goes, hmm.
如果你和珍娜交谈，她发出“嗯”的声音。

1192
00:56:59.980 --> 00:57:03.100
It means she is slightly judging you and disagrees.
